.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH ag-validate-run 1  "run 0.2.0-rc.2" 
.SH NAME
ag\-validate\-run \- Check out the exact candidate tree of a proposal, run a command on it and record a signed attestation of the result
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBag validate run\fR [\fB\-C\fR|\fB\-\-repo\fR] [\fB\-\-as\fR] [\fB\-\-issuer\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-\-env\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fB\-\-check\fR> <\fB\-\-key\fR> <\fIPROPOSAL\fR> <\fICOMMAND\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check out the exact candidate tree of a proposal, run a command on it and record a signed attestation of the result.
.PP
WARNING: the command runs on this machine without a sandbox. This runner is for trusted code and local workflows; use an isolated execution plane for untrusted code.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-C\fR, \fB\-\-repo\fR \fI<DIR>\fR
Operate on the repository at this path (default: discovered from the current directory)
.TP
\fB\-\-check\fR \fI<CHECK>\fR
Check name, as listed in the policy\*(Aqs `required_validations`
.TP
\fB\-\-as\fR \fI<IDENTITY>\fR
Act as this identity (`user:alice`, `agent:bot#run_…`, `service:ci`). Also: AG_IDENTITY
.TP
\fB\-\-key\fR \fI<KEY>\fR
Name of the issuer key created with `ag validate keygen`
.TP
\fB\-\-issuer\fR \fI<ISSUER>\fR
Issuer identity (default: `service:<key name>`)
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON output
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<WHEN>\fR
Colour the output: auto (a terminal, unless NO_COLOR is set), always or never
.TP
\fB\-\-env\fR \fI<ENV>\fR
Environment digest to record (default: derived from the command and platform)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print only what was asked for: no confirmations or hints. Errors and refusals are still shown
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Explain what is happening on standard error: repository, identity, remote, timing
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIPROPOSAL\fR>
Proposal id
.TP
<\fICOMMAND\fR>
The command and its arguments
.SH VERSION
v0.2.0\-rc.2
